#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# gudermannian

#% text
# `gudermannian(x)` gives the Gudermannian function 2 atan(tanh(x/2)).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It relates the circular and hyperbolic functions: `tan(gudermannian(x)/2) = tanh(x/2)`.

#% item
# `gudermannian` is odd.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
gudermannian(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
gudermannian(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.8657694832396586

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
gudermannian(-x)
#% output
#= -gudermannian(x)

#% cell
n(gudermannian(2), 20)
#% output
#= 1.301760336046015099876156

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inverse_gudermannian`, `atan`, `tanh`
